p="docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-21-sma-840-anthropic-thinking-signatures-design.md"
s=open(p).read().rstrip("\n")+"""

### CodeRabbit round 1

The default `ExtendedThinking::Disabled` sends no `thinking` field. On `claude-sonnet-5-5` the model then thinks adaptively, with no `block_binding`. The crate sent the thinking blocks back, and a change of `system` could give HTTP 400 on a new account. Sven chose "replay only if set". With `Disabled`, the translator sends no thinking block back, and the blocks keep the order they had before this PR. `Adaptive` and `Enabled` replay the blocks as before. The review also found that a source that loses its thinking must lose its sort slots, so its blocks keep the plain order. Position data for each text block is deferred to a follow-up issue.
"""
open(p,"w").write(s)
